---
import DocsLayout from '../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout
	title="Responsible use"
	eyebrow="[ POLICY ]"
	description="Kuyfi sends real on-chain transactions to Stellar Testnet. Use it like a pentest tool — with authorization."
>
	<Callout type="danger" title="Authorization required">
		<p>
			Run only against contracts you own or have <strong>explicit written authorization</strong>
			to test. Unauthorized fuzzing of third-party contracts may violate terms of service and
			may be illegal in your jurisdiction.
		</p>
	</Callout>

	<h2>Rules of engagement</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Testnet only — Kuyfi does not support Mainnet in v0.1.0.</li>
		<li>Do not point tooling at Mainnet contracts without the owner’s consent (even with other tools).</li>
		<li>Treat every finding as a lead, not a verdict.</li>
		<li>Do not market Kuyfi output as a formal audit deliverable or certification.</li>
		<li>Do not store or log ephemeral private keys (Kuyfi does not; keep it that way).</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>What Kuyfi does not claim</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>Absence of findings ≠ absence of vulnerabilities</li>
		<li><code>POTENTIAL_VULN</code> ≠ confirmed exploitable bug</li>
		<li>Black-box coverage ≠ full semantic understanding of author intent</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Disclosure</h2>
	<p>
		If you discover a real issue in a third-party contract while authorized to test, follow
		that project’s responsible disclosure process. Kuyfi’s own security issues: open a private
		report via the GitHub repository maintainers.
	</p>

	<p>License: MIT. Not affiliated with the Stellar Development Foundation.</p>
</DocsLayout>
